        {
          "id": "limitation-1",
          "say": "The speed advantage does not automatically extend to very long sequences. The authors note self-attention cost grows with length, so they suggest limiting attention to a neighborhood of size r, which lengthens dependency paths. Do not conclude unrestricted attention stays cheap for arbitrarily long inputs.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "type": "focus",
              "target": "p7.s2"
            },
            {
              "type": "board_clear"
            },
